5. A NOTE ON THE LEGACY POWERBUILDER TREE
===============================================================================

The PowerBuilder sources under ws_objects/, together with the compiled libraries
and target and workspace files (*.pbl, *.pbt, *.pbw, *.pbg, *.pbr, *.pbd), the
frozen PowerBuilder 12.5 tree under oldversion/125/, the consolidated
redistribution libraries under pack/, the native binaries at the repository root,
the resources under res/, the Sciter samples and widgets under samples/sciter/ and
sciter_control/, and the legacy browser assets under tests/blink/, tests/sciter/
and tests/webview/, all remain in this repository deliberately. They are the
behavioural specification for the .NET services and the oracle against which
those services are characterized for parity, so they are treated as read-only and
are not edited, relocated or removed.

The licence terms in sections 1 and 2 apply to them exactly as they always have.
The .NET tree is purely additive: it does not replace, relicense or supersede any
part of the legacy tree, and it depends on neither the PowerBuilder toolchain, nor
the PowerBuilder runtime, nor any of the shipped native binaries.

The same attribution conditions are additionally embedded in the headers of
individual PowerBuilder objects throughout the legacy tree -- for example
ws_objects/pfw.shared.pbl.src/retcode.sru -- which is how the copyright holder
arranged for the conditions to travel with the code itself rather than live only
in a root file. Sections 1 and 2 above are transcribed from the root LICENSE and
README files, which are the canonical statement of those terms.


